  "answer": "I'll start by reading the debugging skill, then trace why special prices with an end date never show up on the storefront API.The failing case is a special that has both dates: the price check treats the start date as the end date, and product save writes the end date into the start field. I'll fix both.Special prices that include an end date were dropped in two places. Saving a product wrote the end date into the special start-date field, and the storefront price calculation required the start date to be both before and after today, so a bounded special never counted as a discount. The end date is now stored on the end-date field, and a special applies when the start date is already in the past and the end date is still ahead.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-core -am test -Dtest=ProductPriceUtilsDiscountTest -DfailIfNoTests=false\"], \"result\": \"passed\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"admin REST create followed by a storefront product read\"], \"missing\": [\"an API-level fixture that posts a product special with an end date and reads it back from the storefront\"]}",
